  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CONSERVATION OF THE LEATHERBACK TURTLE IN MEXICAN PACIFIC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO IMPLEMENT A CONSERVATION PROGRAM FOR THE EAST PACIFIC LEATHERBACK NESTING POPULATION IN MEXICO ON THREE PRIMARY AND TWO SECONDARY NESTING BEACHES TO PROTECT NESTS FROM POACHING, DEPREDATION, AND TIDAL INUNDATION. ACTIVITIES INCLUDE (1) SURVEYING TIERRA COLORADA, CAHUITAN, BARRA DE LA CRUZ, SAN JUAN CHACAHUA, AND BAHA DE CHACAHUA NESTING BEACHES AT NIGHT THROUGHOUT THE NESTING SEASON TO DETER POACHING AND COUNT NESTS TO MONITOR NESTING TRENDS AND (2) RELOCATING NESTS THREATENED BY POACHING AND TIDAL INUNDATION TO SECURE BEACH HATCHERIES.</narrative>
  </description>
